---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Exterior Painting in Florida Humidity | When to Paint & How Long It Lasts"
  description="Best practices for exterior painting in Central Florida's humidity. Drying times, paint selection, and how to avoid blistering and mildew."
  ogImage="/images/bedroom-paint.jpg"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/exterior-painting-florida-humidity/#article",
        "headline": "Exterior Painting in Florida Humidity",
        "description": "How Florida humidity affects exterior painting. Best seasons, prep, and paint selection for long-lasting results.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/exterior-painting-florida-humidity/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Exterior Painting Florida Humidity",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/exterior-painting-florida-humidity"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Exterior Painting Florida Humidity</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Exterior Painting in Florida Humidity</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        When to paint, how long it lasts, and how to avoid blistering and mildew in Central Florida's climate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            Florida's year-round humidity makes <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">exterior painting</a> trickier than cooler, drier climates. Paint that lasts 10 years in Colorado might fail in 5-7 years here. Here's how to paint exterior surfaces in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida so it holds up.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How Humidity Affects Exterior Paint</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Slower Drying Times</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Paint needs to dry between coats and before rain hits. High humidity slows evaporation, which means longer wait times. If you apply a second coat too soon, trapped moisture can cause blistering or poor adhesion.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Mildew Growth</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Mildew thrives in Florida's moisture. It grows on painted surfaces—especially north-facing walls that stay damp and shaded. Cheap paint without mildewcide turns green and black within a year. Quality exterior paint includes additives that resist mildew.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Paint Failure from Moisture Intrusion</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            If moisture gets trapped behind paint (from poor prep or rain shortly after painting), it pushes the paint off the surface. You'll see peeling, bubbling, or flaking—usually within 1-2 years. Proper surface prep and timing prevent this.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Florida fact:</strong> Central Florida has 60-80% humidity most of the year, with daily afternoon thunderstorms in summer. Timing your paint job around weather is critical—more so than in drier climates.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Best Time to Paint Exteriors in Central Florida</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">October through April (Best)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Cooler, drier months with less rain. Lower humidity speeds drying, and you have longer weather windows between storms. This is peak season for exterior painting in Florida—book early.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">May through September (Risky)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            High heat, high humidity, and daily afternoon thunderstorms. Paint dries slower, and sudden rain can ruin fresh coats. We can work in summer if weather cooperates, but it requires careful scheduling and weather monitoring. Expect delays if storms roll in.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Surface Prep is Everything</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Florida's humidity, sun, and mildew are hard on exterior surfaces. Proper prep is the difference between paint that lasts 7 years and paint that peels in 2. Here's what matters:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Power Wash Before Painting</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Dirt, mildew, and loose paint must be removed before new paint goes on. We <a href="/services/power-washing" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">power wash</a> all exterior surfaces, then wait 24-48 hours for them to dry completely. Skipping this step causes new paint to peel fast. Read more about <a href="/guides/power-washing-before-painting-florida" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">power washing before painting</a>.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Scrape & Sand Loose Paint</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Old paint that's peeling or bubbling needs to be scraped off. We sand edges smooth so you don't see ridges through the new coat. Painting over loose paint just causes the new layer to fail.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Prime Bare Spots & Stains</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Any bare wood, patched <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall</a>, or stucco needs primer before paint. Water stains and tannin bleed also need stain-blocking primer (Kilz or BIN). Skipping primer causes uneven color and poor adhesion.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Caulk Gaps & Cracks</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Gaps around windows, doors, trim, and siding let water in. We caulk all seams with paintable, flexible caulk that moves with the home as it expands and contracts in Florida heat. This prevents moisture intrusion and paint failure.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Choosing the Right Paint for Florida</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Not all exterior paint is rated for Florida's climate. Here's what to look for:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">100% Acrylic Latex (Best)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            High-quality acrylic latex paint breathes, resists mildew, and holds up in UV and humidity. Brands like Sherwin-Williams Duration, Benjamin Moore Aura, or Behr Marquee are proven in Florida. We use these on most homes.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Mildewcide Additives</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Look for paint labeled "mildew resistant" or "contains mildewcide." This is critical for north-facing walls, shaded siding, and homes near lakes or heavy tree coverage. Without it, green and black stains appear within a year.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">UV Resistance</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Florida sun fades paint faster than northern climates. Quality exterior paint includes UV-blocking pigments that slow fading. Cheap paint fades to chalky pastels in 2-3 years.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Skip Cheap Builder-Grade Paint</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Bargain paint might save you $100 upfront, but it'll cost you $3,000 in repainting when it fails in 3 years instead of 7. We use mid to high-grade paint on every job—it's the difference between a warranty we stand behind and one we're repainting under.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Exterior Surfaces in Central Florida</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Stucco</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Common in Florida homes. Stucco absorbs moisture and cracks over time, especially in older homes. We repair cracks, prime, and use elastomeric or high-build acrylic paint that flexes with the stucco. Read more about <a href="/guides/stucco-and-humidity-central-florida" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">stucco and humidity</a>.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Vinyl Siding</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Vinyl can be painted if it's faded or you want a color change. We clean thoroughly, use vinyl-safe paint, and avoid dark colors (they absorb heat and warp vinyl). Light to medium colors work best.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Wood & Hardie Board</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Wood siding needs primer on bare spots and caulking at all seams. Hardie board (fiber cement) is more forgiving but still needs proper prep. Both hold paint well if prepped right.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How Long Does Exterior Paint Last in Florida?</h2>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Quality paint, proper prep:</strong> 7-10 years</li>
            <li><strong>Mid-grade paint, proper prep:</strong> 5-7 years</li>
            <li><strong>Cheap paint or poor prep:</strong> 2-4 years (then it peels and fails)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Regular <a href="/services/power-washing" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">power washing</a> (every 12-18 months) extends paint life by removing mildew and dirt before they degrade the finish. Touch-ups on trim and high-wear areas also help.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Exterior Painting Mistakes in Florida</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Painting over mildew:</strong> Mildew grows through new paint. Always power wash first.</li>
            <li><strong>Painting in summer rain:</strong> Rain within 4 hours of painting ruins the coat. We monitor weather closely.</li>
            <li><strong>Skipping primer:</strong> Bare wood, stucco, or stains need primer. Paint alone won't stick or cover properly.</li>
            <li><strong>Rushing between coats:</strong> High humidity slows drying. Applying a second coat too soon causes blistering.</li>
            <li><strong>Using cheap paint:</strong> Saving $100 on paint costs $3,000 when it fails in 3 years.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What to Expect When You Hire Us</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We've painted hundreds of <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida exteriors. Here's how we handle Florida's humidity:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Power wash first:</strong> Remove mildew, dirt, and loose paint</li>
            <li><strong>Wait for surfaces to dry:</strong> 24-48 hours depending on humidity</li>
            <li><strong>Scrape, sand, and prime:</strong> Proper prep on every surface</li>
            <li><strong>Use quality paint:</strong> Mildew-resistant, UV-rated, proven in Florida</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor weather:</strong> We watch forecasts and adjust schedules to avoid rain</li>
            <li><strong>Two coats minimum:</strong> One coat doesn't hold up in Florida sun and humidity</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="text-center mt-12">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-6 font-sans">Ready to paint your Central Florida home's exterior?</p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Exterior Painting That Lasts in Florida's Climate"
    description="Quality prep, quality paint, and proper timing. Serving Central Florida."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
